WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.450
He swept floors at JCPenney

2
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.950
and wore a thrift-store coat.

3
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:04.100
When he died,

4
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.300
he left $8 million

5
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.100
to a library and a hospital.

6
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.200
His name was Ronald Read,

7
00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.600
and he ran a gas station for decades.

8
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.350
He drove an old Toyota

9
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.850
and held his coat together

10
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.050
with a safety pin.

11
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.800
Nobody in his town knew

12
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.600
he owned shares in 95 companies.

13
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.400
He never picked winners.

14
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.150
He just bought good companies

15
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.350
and never sold them.

16
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.050
He started buying stocks in the 1950s

17
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.550
with money from his paycheck.

18
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.000
He bought blue-chip names

19
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:31.800
like P&G and Johnson & Johnson.

20
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.250
He reinvested every dividend,

21
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.150
year after year,

22
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.350
for about 60 years.

23
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:36.500
By 2014,

24
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.400
those small buys

25
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:38.900
had grown into $8 million.

26
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:41.000
Wealth isn't about earning more.

27
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.200
It's about buying steadily

28
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.400
and not touching it.

29
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.450
Time did the work he couldn't.

30
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:46.950
I'm Dimples.

31
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.050
I talk about the things we feel

32
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.550
but never say out loud.

33
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.450
Follow for more.
